# PONS $101 — OPEN-SOURCE GOVERNANCE, CONTRIBUTION & LICENSING

PONS $101 is designed to be inspected, challenged, extended, reproduced, and improved.

The repository is not intended to become a black-box token launcher.

It is intended to become an auditable research laboratory in which:

HUMANS

AI AGENTS

DEVELOPERS

RESEARCHERS

AUDITORS

STUDENTS

PROTOCOL ENGINEERS

and

INDEPENDENT REVIEWERS

can understand what the system does, why it does it, which assumptions it makes, and what evidence supports its conclusions.

The contribution doctrine is:

IMPROVE THE SYSTEM.

DO NOT WEAKEN THE EVIDENCE.

AUTOMATE THE REPEATABLE.

DO NOT AUTOMATE AWAY HUMAN AUTHORITY.

==================================================
CONTRIBUTION OBJECTIVE
==================================================

Contributions are encouraged when they improve:

• reproducibility
• security
• documentation
• event indexing
• contract adapters
• experiment schemas
• fee interpretation
• behavioral research
• mixed-methods analysis
• agent orchestration
• testing
• dashboards
• Discord integration
• provenance
• public-good accounting
• external review
• educational usefulness

A contribution should not be judged only by:

HOW MUCH CODE DID IT ADD?

The stronger question is:

DID IT MAKE THE EXPERIMENT MORE RELIABLE, MORE TRANSPARENT, OR MORE REPRODUCIBLE?

==================================================
HUMAN AUTHORITY
==================================================

The human operator remains the final signer.

An agent may:

recommend

prepare

simulate

